---
const parts = [
  [
    "Premiere panel",
    "CEP 11 + ExtendScript. Reads the timeline each second, sends what changed, applies what your partner sent.",
  ],
  [
    "Sync engine",
    "Plain JavaScript with no Premiere calls, tested on its own with node --test.",
  ],
  [
    "Relay",
    "Node.js + ws on the host laptop. Numbers every edit; the higher revision wins.",
  ],
  [
    "Live cursor",
    "A PowerShell helper draws a click-through overlay with your partner's pointer and name.",
  ],
];
---

<section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <h2 id="how-title" class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      parts.map(([title, text], i) => (
        <li class="card border-base-300 border">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-primary text-sm font-bold" aria-hidden="true">0{i + 1}</span>
            <h3 class="card-title">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm">{text}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
  <p class="mt-6">
    Laptops connect over <strong>Tailscale</strong>, so it works on any network
    with internet. If two edits touch the same field, the latest numbered edit
    wins on both machines.
  </p>
</section>
